            <div xml:id="d421">

                <pb facs="0475" n="463" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg463"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.00/2109: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-11-06T14:00:00-03:00">November 6, 1943—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2630. Embassy’s telegram No. 2610, November 3, 8 p.m.<anchor n="59"
                        xml:id="d421-f1"/> Various delegations of army officers estimated by <hi
                        rendition="#italic">El Pueblo</hi> to number about 300 persons, visited the
                    Foreign Minister yesterday afternoon to express their complete support of his
                    recent declarations to correspondent of Santiago newspaper <hi
                        rendition="#italic">El Mercurio</hi> that the policy of Argentina is one of
                    complete and absolute neutrality.</p>
                <p>Foregoing item is carried in all papers and was evidently officially
                    inspired.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Embassy at Santiago.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Armour</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
